    "id": "p6-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "A tradesman is making the wooden rectangular frame for a gate. In order to make the frame stronger and to keep it square, the tradesman will put a diagonal piece into the frame as shown in the diagram.\n\nIf the frame is 1.2 m wide and 2 m high, find the length of the diagonal piece of wood, in metres, correct to 3 decimal places.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p6-q8-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "\\begin{tikzpicture}[line join=round,line width=0.8pt,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont]\n\\draw[black](0,0)rectangle(1.2,2);\\draw[black](0,2)--(1.2,0);\n\\draw[black,line width=.4pt](0,.12)--(.12,.12)--(.12,0) (0,1.88)--(.12,1.88)--(.12,2) (1.08,2)--(1.08,1.88)--(1.2,1.88) (1.08,0)--(1.08,.12)--(1.2,.12);\n\\path(0,2)--(1.2,2)node[midway,above]{1.2 m};\\path(1.2,0)--(1.2,2)node[midway,right]{2 m};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
